{"c":[{"id":"4e94ccf8ea0486ea","sum":"G2-P4: never widen restates(); say 'at 3pm'; no default chat route; page plans set WindowSel.page; host page focus only from pageField; recheckFields drops failing fields only; page-link patches writes; window-left skips the browser; tab-left text via TabSource.viewFor.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5ac6125c74b45908","sum":"G2-P2: never widen restates(); guest fixture at x=0; say 'at 3pm'; no default chat route. Page plans set WindowSel.page, page focus from pageField; tests never read GROQ_API_KEY; recheckFields drops only failing fields.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"afbc0885430f4042","sum":"G2-L1: never widen restates(); D2-06 scene 2 ends partial live. Guest fixture at x=0; no '--' in .entitlements; say 'at 3pm'; probe an EKEventStore if status flaps. No default chat route (--dev-writer); Gemma drafts few-shot.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"fdc428b470104795","sum":"G2-H8: restates() is a closed clause-suffix rule, never widen it; live Jev leaves D2-06 scene 2 partial. Guest 960x600: fixture to x=0; no '--' in .entitlements comments; event ⌘Z only after a verified step.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"6c27db8da975f9b4","sum":"G2: drafts.ts restates() is a closed clause-suffix rule; looser versions had 5 bypasses, never widen it. Live Jev confirmed Order number but not a reply's To sender or a derived event, so D2-06 scene 2 ends partial (evidence/screen/g2).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T173413Z-41b9cc8b0f0c0c83","text":"G2: drafts.ts restates() (skip Jev for a restated sentence) is a closed-frame clause-suffix rule; two reviews found 5 bypasses in looser versions (token sets, 'Avoid saying', 'NOT saying', 'provided'); never widen it by adding words.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T180513Z-82a90a8786c261a8","text":"G2: live Jev (Ask's yes/no value question, 0.75 floor) confirmed Order number but not a reply's sender in To or a derived calendar event for 'add this meeting to my calendar and draft a reply to Priya', so D2-06 scene 2 ends partial live; see evidence/screen/g2 jev-*-probe.txt.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"6064b9b210ca22b7","sum":"H8: guest is 960x600 pt, move a centred caret-fixture to x=0 or event cards find noClearSpot; seed-user-tcc.sh restarts tccd; no '--' in .entitlements comments; event card ⌘Z only after a verified step; calendar adds report written:0.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T182018Z-0c929a2ce63bdaff","text":"H8 VM: the rig guest is 960x600 pt; a centred caret-fixture executor window leaves every event-card spot covering a field (noClearSpot): move it to x=0 (fixture-ax move). seed-user-tcc.sh restarts tccd: running it while a TCC prompt is up shows the prompt twice.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T182018Z-327bc9cdd4327c33","text":"H8: an XML comment in an .entitlements file must not contain '--' (AMFIUnserializeXML refuses it and codesign fails). The event card's done line takes ⌘Z only after a verified step; the helper reports written:0 for calendar adds.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f5079ae2f5b9473e","sum":"H8-L1: say 'at 3pm' (an open AM/PM makes no event card); EKEventStore status can flap, probe a store. No default chat route; --dev-writer names one. Gemma E2B is a base model (few-shot drafts); deadlineMs is epoch ms.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"1c1ae9c575164268","sum":"H8: 'Thursday at 3' makes no event card since D2-03 (say 'at 3pm'); a card with no end asks how long. EKEventStore.authorizationStatus can flap notDetermined after a grant; host and reader probe a store instead.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T182018Z-f0560794b2ec28fa","text":"H8: since D2-03 an event sentence whose time leaves AM/PM open ('Thursday at 3') makes no event card; use 'at 3pm'. onscreen_acceptance.py still types 'at 3'. A card from a time with no end asks how long (30 min first, Tab takes it).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T182023Z-1d9814a513f71781","text":"H8: in a process running when Calendar access was granted, EKEventStore.authorizationStatus flapped notDetermined/fullAccess (VM) while a new store's calendars(for:) read fine; host and reader probe a store when status says notDetermined (no prompt).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f38309cb9958372d","sum":"L1: no chat route by default (writer routes null); a developer names groq:<model> or gateway:<model> via --dev-writer. Gemma E2B is a base model, so local drafts are few-shot; caret-local-model needs a grammar; deadlineMs is epoch ms.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T201333Z-b3e261779dc6c92b","text":"L1: no chat route is a default (WRITER_ROUTE and INTENT_ROUTE null, ASK_MAKER jev); a developer names one as groq:<model> or gateway:<model> (writer/routes.ts) with the helper's --dev-writer or an eval script's writer flag.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T201333Z-fdcac01d5471b677","text":"L1: Cotypist's Gemma E2B is a base model, so local draft prompts are few-shot documents (writer/local-draft.ts); caret-local-model refuses a request with no grammar. localTextRequest.deadlineMs is epoch ms, not a duration.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"00fd5ab66bea54da","sum":"H10-P2: page plans set WindowSel.page; host reads page focus from pageField only; label >80 blocks saved answers. Tests never read GROQ_API_KEY; new Ask makers join oneAnswer; recheckFields drops only failing fields.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"637b36e430ed09a4","sum":"H10-S1: page plans set WindowSel.page (page and reader windows share id and title); host reads page focus only from pageField. labelTooLong (label >80) blocks saved answers; old hosts lost the memory list on the answers doc id.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"1de8a2f92e9f1531","sum":"H10: a page window and its browser's reader window share bundle id and title, so page plans set WindowSel.page. Chrome shows AX no web content or focus, so the host reads page focus and frames only from pageField (PageFocusSource).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T203747Z-1771ea16bd50b7ed","text":"H10: a page window and the reader's window of the same browser share bundle id and title; plans for a page must set WindowSel.page or they stop as ambiguous.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T203747Z-8582de2538fa78c4","text":"H10: Chrome shows Accessibility no web content and no focused element while a page field has focus (VM probe), so the host reads page focus and frames only from the helper's pageField (PageFocusSource).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"4168398783b277b0","sum":"S1: fill throws labelTooLong for a focused label over 80 chars on a page with little prose, so no saved answer there. Hosts before H11 refused the answers doc id and lost the whole memory list; answers.md is listed only to savedAnswers hosts.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T204550Z-12e324b0b44784bf","text":"Fill throws labelTooLong when the focused field's label is over 80 chars on a page with little other prose (privacy prose share); saved answers can't be offered there.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T204550Z-3e3d4d7a0bdec136","text":"Hosts before v2/answers throw on an unknown memoryDocument id, losing the whole memory list; the server lists answers.md only to hosts with the savedAnswers capability.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d6e449e5f141c6b0","sum":"P1-P2: tests never read GROQ_API_KEY (no-groq.ts); a new Ask maker joins planAsk's oneAnswer gate; recheckFields drops only a failing field; derived parts keep their line's label as context, else need an equal line.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"796fd5afdca57f46","sum":"P1: no-groq.ts fails any test reading GROQ_API_KEY even if caught (pass env objects). On W4 Greenhouse, recheckFill refused Fill all: a derived Country part needs a line equal to the span for a control with no label context.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T205140Z-7ef033e31edcf1b4","text":"P1: helper/test/setup/no-groq.ts (vitest setupFiles) fails any test file that reads process.env.GROQ_API_KEY, even if the throw is caught; pass explicit env objects to readKey/writersOnStart in tests.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T205140Z-d6ebebc54b7a4ea1","text":"P1: on W4's saved Greenhouse pages Fill all is refused whole by recheckFill (offers/fill-popup.ts ~218): Country 'United States' is a derived part of 'Location: Oakland, California, United States (...)', and a control without label context needs a line equal to the span.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"59654fc6f3466291","sum":"P1-P2: the heads maker is one answer, so planAsk gates it like the writer; a new maker name must join that gate. A derived part carries its line's label as context; recheckFields drops only the failing field; sourceHolds re-derives spans.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T205140Z-f4ebc7703c97844e","text":"P1: the heads Ask maker (planner/intent-heads.ts) is one answer, so planAsk gates it like the writer (oneAnswer = makerName !== 'jev': inferredAll, listsAll, confirmScope); a new maker name must be added to that gate or its scope stands unconfirmed.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T220819Z-519d2cf2c3af807c","text":"P2: a fill part derived from one 'Label: value' line carries that label as FillHandoff.context; recheckFields drops a field that fails its recheck and runs the rest; an unlabelled span inside a longer line passes only if derive.ts re-derives it (fill-popup.ts sourceHolds).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"9199063a79210b69","sum":"P2-P4 pages: page-link patches a verified write (one trailing walk); page Asks plan in page-planner.ts; window-left skips the browser's reader window; check undo over CDP; mergeCutWalk keeps unsent nodes; tab-left text only via TabSource.viewFor; freeze goldens via zod.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"04e70b9b4b65451f","sum":"P2-C1 pages: page-link patches a written control (one trailing walk); page Asks plan in page-planner.ts (clones refused); CfT calls Google via any proxy; guest Mail has no account; window-left skips the browser's reader window; check undo over CDP; goals leave restored picks.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c4886c398087e862","sum":"P2-H10: page-link patches a verified write, walks once TRAILING_WALK_MS later; page Asks plan in page-planner.ts (gate 'fill' by identity: clones refused); headless CfT calls Google via any proxy (F1: browserService); guest Mail has no account (.eml: Add Account).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"353d6de786750cc3","sum":"P2: page-link patches a written control and walks once TRAILING_WALK_MS after the last act. A page Ask is planned by page-planner.ts with no writer; gate 'fill' is marked by identity, so propose refuses a structuredClone'd plan.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T220819Z-878907191e2eb647","text":"P2: engines/page-link.ts no longer walks after a verified pageWrite/pageSelect/pageSetChecked; it patches that control in the tab's last walk and walks once TRAILING_WALK_MS after the last act. Tests that expected a pageWalk after an ok write must expect the patch.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T220819Z-d4c70d849120ef71","text":"P2: an Ask about a page (goals:true) comes back as AskGoal.page and is planned by goals/page-planner.ts with no writer; its steps are gate 'fill', which only lowering marks (gates.ts markFilled, by identity), so GoalRuns.propose refuses a structuredClone'd page plan.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"dc7a4168ce70092a","sum":"F1-H10: headless CfT calls Google hosts through any proxy; the F1 sink files them as browserService(), not offsite(). The rig guest's Mail has no account (an .eml shows Add Account; its buttons label in AXDescription).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T224055Z-4008dd64a8214ebf","text":"Headless Chrome for Testing keeps calling Google hosts (google.com, googleapis.com) through a proxy whatever flags it gets; the F1 network sink (fixtures/web-form/oracle.ts) files them under browserService(), not offsite().","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T235610Z-e61928d562069b22","text":"H10: in the rig guest Mail has no account: opening an .eml shows the Add Account sheet, not the message; its SwiftUI buttons carry their label in AXDescription, not AXTitle.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2eaf29a830280b84","sum":"H10-C1: a page's window just left skips its browser's reader window; F1's probe lags the DOM (check undo over CDP); 'from my notes' reads one resolved window; goal runs leave a restored combobox pick to the user and skip its dependents.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"62823ecfd9d9074a","sum":"H10-F1: a page's window just left skips its browser's own reader window (else Jev withheld at 0.65-0.77); F1's probe can lag the DOM after a burst of writes, so check undo by reading the DOM over CDP (page-loop-eval DOM_VALUES_JS).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T235611Z-1dede3bef7f49f2e","text":"H10: a page's 'window just left' (ScreenModel.windowBefore) skips the reader's window of the same browser; without that, Jev withheld page fills at 0.65-0.77.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T005116Z-802d1a3e98c70699","text":"F1's probe posts state with fetch keepalive and drops a failed post after recording it sent, so after a burst of writes the oracle can lag the DOM; page-loop-eval checks undo by reading the DOM over CDP (DOM_VALUES_JS).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0a881e10261f1993","sum":"P2-C1: 'from my notes' makes an Ask read only the window it resolves to (a decoy on the corpus); goal runs leaveFailedToYou: a restored combobox pick is listed (Executor.leftToYou) and dependents (state/city/ZIP) skipped; other callers stop.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T005116Z-d31529fbf9335d38","text":"P2 evals: an Ask saying 'from my notes' makes code read only the one window it resolves that to (planner/sources.ts); on the corpus that was a decoy note. Page-loop goal runs ask 'fill out this form', which heads settles as a whole form.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T021405Z-957fa1314ab52f39","text":"C1: goal segments run with leaveFailedToYou: a combobox pick the page put back (VerbResult restored) and read back unchanged is listed via Executor.leftToYou and the run goes on, skipping a country's state/city/ZIP (executor/dependents.ts). Other callers still stop.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2dd914a0e2eed67d","sum":"P3-C1: mergeCutWalk keeps unsent nodes; attach rows for goalFiles hosts; carries span pages; says.ts never names Jev; freeze goldens via zod; tab-left text only via TabSource.viewFor; CfT tab switch via worker; fill budget load-dependent (budgetMs Infinity).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"777a097740a458a3","sum":"P3: cut walks keep unsent nodes (mergeCutWalk); attach rows only for goalFiles hosts, confirmedFile names its step; a carry lives across pages (carryOn); says.ts never names Jev; freeze golden lines through their zod schema (keys in schema order).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b3b6ceb345ada2a0","sum":"P3: a cut reader walk keeps prior unsent nodes until a complete walk (model.ts mergeCutWalk); page goals get attach rows only for a goalFiles host (helper.ts filesFor); confirmedFile names the attach step; rows with no file drop from the run (runs.ts stepMap).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T021729Z-2e26e31d9e56986f","text":"P3: a cut reader walk (root null, stats.truncated) keeps every prior node it did not send until a complete walk (model.ts mergeCutWalk); inferring 'passed' nodes from the old order dropped a text area that a moved node jumped ahead of. Pages are still replaced whole.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T021733Z-eb34e4009fe61d9d","text":"P3: page goals get attach rows only for a host with goalFiles (helper.ts filesFor; in process via HelperOptions.goalFiles); goalAccept.confirmedFile names the attach step, and rows given no file are dropped from the run (runs.ts stepMap maps executor steps back to segment steps).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b342efa209afe515","sum":"P3: a carry lives across pages until its goal finishes (runs.ts carryOn; pageWalked leaves a carried document alone); says.ts never names Jev ('Caret's model'); freeze golden lines through their zod schema (parse writes keys in schema order).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T021750Z-652b23e48a36082a","text":"P3: a carry lives across pages until a carried goal finishes (runs.ts carryOn); GoalRuns.carrying(windowId, doc) is true only for the document a carry plans, so helper.ts pageWalked leaves that page alone and takes any page the carry planned nothing for.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T021800Z-55351013aa4fbe71","text":"P3: user sentences in planner/says.ts never name Jev (test/says.test.ts plain()); Jev failure sentences say 'Caret's model'. Golden lines must be normalised through their zod schema before freezing: parse writes keys in schema order, so a round trip of a hand-built line differs.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c9f2c23e721be85d","sum":"P4-C1: tab-left text only via TabSource.viewFor(owner), never ScreenModel; CfT tab switches via chrome.tabs/windows.update in the worker (switchTo); fill's 15 ms budget makes probes load-dependent (budgetMs Infinity); line values read in TS (line-values.ts).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"298edb042298a31c","sum":"P4: text read from the tab left never enters ScreenModel; only fill sees it via TabSource.viewFor(owner). Headless CfT tab switches the extension sees: chrome.tabs.update + chrome.windows.update in the worker over the DevTools pipe (tab-source-journey.ts switchTo).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T032217Z-1ff9070e78c5cbc1","text":"P4: text read from the tab the user just left never enters ScreenModel; only fill paths see it, via TabSource.viewFor(owner) (engines/tab-source.ts). Never hand helper.model views or TabSource nodes to other consumers (router, event cards, shadow, transfers).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T032245Z-9aff69e636408257","text":"P4: headless CfT tab switches that the extension's tabs/windows listeners really see: evaluate chrome.tabs.update + chrome.windows.update in the extension worker over the DevTools pipe (fixtures/web-form/tab-source-journey.ts switchTo).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"05ed1f5f8cad4a0d","sum":"C1: fill's candidate budget (15 ms wall clock) makes in-process probes load-dependent (45-62 proposed under load ~30): compare at like load or pass budgetMs Infinity; fill reads values inside lines in TS (line-values.ts); recheck counts code-found ones via lineGives.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T032641Z-108c3beb10547e40","text":"C1: the candidate generator's 15 ms wall-clock budget makes in-process fill probes load-dependent: the corpus probe swung 45-62 proposed under load avg ~30; compare runs only at like load, or pass budgetMs Infinity.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T032641Z-52a641b0527a12b8","text":"C1: fill reads values inside lines in TS (fill/line-values.ts, candidates.ts windowValues), so the page-loop eval's replayed sources (values: []) now get typed values as the reader would give them; the recheck counts only reader values as typed, code-found ones via lineGives.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"387c54cf2e06fe08","sum":"C1-H13 + fill lore: page plans end in a row:true hand-off; host.sock in <home>/sockets; page offers are OfferSource.page; memoryRefOf refs; big forms fill in parts; Laya fixture-only; with-heavy: disk minus est >= 8 GiB, no lockf build.lock inside; closeTyping for undo.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"bcd860fe20ff53b5","sum":"C1-J1, H11-H13: page plans end in a hand-off row; host.sock is in <home>/sockets; Jev has a daily cap (CARET_JEV_DAILY_CAP); inject test pageFields over the debug socket; page offers are OfferSource.page and Tab sends pageInsert; never lockf build.lock in with-heavy.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"37e4af8adcf8abcf","sum":"C1-H12: WARNS-word sentences go whole; page plans end with a row:true hand-off; Asks read the tab left only at fill/pagePlan; host.sock in <home>/sockets (CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full); .fixedSize(horizontal:) clips wraps; no lockf build.lock in with-heavy.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"cd14b8843dd9d3ee","sum":"C1-I6: a WARNS-word sentence goes whole or not at all; page plans end with a row:true hand-off (no executor step); an Ask reads the tab left only at its fill step or pagePlan; ambient fill leaves a goal's page alone; the hourly budget holds pageWalked.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"2691af9702ea9f68","sum":"C1-I6: a value whose sentence holds a WARNS word goes with it as a required clause or not at all; page plans end with a row:true hand-off step ('You press <label>' / 'The rest is yours') with no executor step, so seg.plan.steps is one shorter.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T032641Z-df47ef2e50ca5a79","text":"C1: a value whose own sentence holds a WARNS word goes with that sentence as a required clause or not at all; sentence ends are conservative (lowercase word or digit before, capital after). Whole-line clauses cost corpus clinic-intake two values.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T062218Z-bb39f9f0467bc5ce","text":"I6: page plans end with a GoalStep row:true (kind handoff, 'You press <label>' or 'The rest is yours'); it is always the last step, lower.ts gives it no executor step, so seg.plan.steps is one shorter than seg.steps.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"740e3d49bc3a2762","sum":"I6: an Ask reads the tab left only at planAsk's fill step or pagePlan (owner: offer key or goal id); ambient fill leaves a goal's page alone (goalOnPage); the hourly budget (balanced 4) holds pageWalked, so the load journey lifts offersPerHour.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T062227Z-47ccc650cd567ff8","text":"I6: an Ask's tab read happens only at planAsk's fill step (fillModel) or in pagePlan; owners are the offer key or goal id; ambient fill/ready-on-load leave a page with a planning/awaiting/running goal alone (goalOnPage) and TabSource refuses an ambient read over a pinned goal.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T062227Z-6c026cce4f5fd842","text":"I6: page-loop-eval runs every page in one helper; the hourly offer budget (balanced 4) holds pageWalked before the ready-on-load check, so the load journey lifts offersPerHour; fill.load_held_<rule> counts holds.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c154314373edc26c","sum":"H11-H12: host.sock in <home>/sockets, release answers state+spend unless CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full; route page-engine test apply to its own helper; .fixedSize(horizontal:) clips wrapped panels (exact width); never lockf build.lock inside with-heavy.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5e0b1d7fe48d167f","sum":"H12-I6: host.sock is <home>/sockets/host.sock; release builds answer only state and spend unless CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full (harnesses setenv it); onboarding auto only without --home/--settings; helper page-engine tests route apply to their own helper.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T035452Z-68fb99dd307065d5","text":"H12: host.sock moved to <home>/sockets/host.sock (default CaretV2/sockets); release builds answer only state (allowlist) and spend unless CARET_DEBUG_SOCKET=full, so release-build harnesses must setenv it. Onboarding defaults to auto only without --home/--settings.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T062227Z-7e02cffa1979776c","text":"I6: helper tests with a page engine must route its apply to their own helper (capture it in a local); a shared 'helper' variable lets an earlier test's trailing walk land in the next test's model.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"86a6db3d2adf8e6a","sum":"H11: under .fixedSize(horizontal: true) wrapped text measures as one line and panels clip: use an exact .frame(width:) with vertical fixedSize; build.lock is a symlink to heavy.lock, so lockf build.lock inside with-heavy deadlocks.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T063851Z-1e89e23b19f1384e","text":"H11: a SwiftUI view under .fixedSize(horizontal: true) is measured at its ideal width, so wrapped text counts as one line and the panel clips its top and bottom; give it an exact .frame(width:) and fixedSize(vertical) only (PopupView PopupWidth).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T063851Z-3a51e09ec56311ba","text":"H11: ~/.caret-run/locks/build.lock is a symlink to ~/.long-run/locks/heavy.lock; wrapping lockf build.lock inside with-heavy.sh (which holds heavy.lock) deadlocks while holding the heavy lease.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1ef09e53bf12acfa","sum":"J1-H13: Jev confidence (p_max-1/n)/(1-1/n); daily cap throws JevCapError; replay cache fixture-only; no distilling Jev output; test pageFields via the host debug socket; page inline offers are OfferSource.page; launchd argv0 is relative.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d174639a9c85f705","sum":"J1: Jev confidence is (p_max - 1/n)/(1 - 1/n); a daily spend cap (CARET_JEV_DAILY_CAP $0.50) throws JevCapError; the replay cache takes fixture text only; TypeSafe's MCA s2.3(b) forbids distilling Jev output.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"987e4b1534648136","sum":"J1: Jev confidence is (p_max - 1/n)/(1 - 1/n) over n options (not the top-two margin judge.ts says; equal only for n=2); makeJevClient holds a per-day spend cap (CARET_JEV_DAILY_CAP, default $0.50) and throws JevCapError; vitest uses a temp spend dir.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T065440Z-6320f5713756d4a4","text":"J1: TypeSafe documents Jev's Choice confidence as (p_max - 1/n)/(1 - 1/n) over n options (docs.typesafe.ai/confidence), not the top-two margin routing/judge.ts describes; the two agree only for two options. engines/decide/confidence.ts computes other engines' confidence this way.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T065544Z-2b923d2a58b8f2cf","text":"J1: makeJevClient holds every request against a per-day spend file (CARET_JEV_DAILY_CAP, default $0.50; CARET_JEV_SPEND_DIR) and throws JevCapError (kind cap) past it; vitest.config.ts points the spend dir at a temp dir.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0d659675b89b1bba","sum":"J1: the replay cache and --log-requests take only fixture text (harness lists fixture window ids; the helper refuses the cache); TypeSafe's MCA s2.3(b) forbids distilling Jev output: train local models on Caret's answer keys or a permissive teacher.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T065553Z-29f2d5c421092ef7","text":"J1: the replay cache (engines/decide/cache.ts) and --log-requests take only fixture text: a harness lists its fixture window ids and says if its memory and plan text (window id 'plan') are fixtures; charged windows are checked too. The helper refuses CARET_JEV_CACHE.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T065553Z-310f47ee41817c11","text":"J1: TypeSafe's Master Customer Agreement s2.3(b) (2026-09-23) forbids using Jev's Output for distillation or to train an imitating model; train a local model on Caret's answer keys or a permissive teacher instead.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"1e39825f89d0ff0d","sum":"H12-H13: inject a test pageField via the host debug socket (the bundled helper gets allowlisted env only); page inline offers are OfferSource.page and Tab sends pageInsert; a note window needs its own app in helper tests; launchd's argv0 is relative.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"379ec0af76ae5f62","sum":"H13: the bundled helper gets only allowlisted env (ServiceLauncher), so inject a test pageField via the host debug socket; page inline offers are OfferSource.page (native ghost clears skip them), insertsText false, and Tab sends pageInsert.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T080508Z-2110f7480275cbcf","text":"H13: the bundled helper gets only allowlisted env (ServiceLauncher: HOME, USER, LANG, TYPESAFE_API_KEY, CARET_ENV_FILE...), so a helper-side test switch never reaches it from Caret.app; inject a pageField through the host debug socket instead.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T080508Z-bc4a09143ef1ff5b","text":"H13: page inline offers use OfferSource.page (never .engine), so HostCoordinator's ghost clears on AX focus changes leave them alone; Claim.insertsText is false for a page ghost and PageInlineMachine sends pageInsert.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"940d166167db3d8d","sum":"H12-H13: launchd starts the agent with relative argv0 'Contents/MacOS/Caret' (use launchctl print's pid or lsof); in helper tests a non-page window with the browser's pid is passed over as Chrome's toolbar, so give a note window its own app.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T080508Z-ed6af011d8df3dcf","text":"H13: in helper tests, a non-page window sharing the page's browser pid is passed over as Chrome's toolbar (H10 ScreenModel.windowBefore); give a note window its own app (NOTES_APP) or TabSource reads the wrong tab.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T082217Z-6e9f887494c1affe","text":"H12: launchd starts the SMAppService agent as relative argv0 'Contents/MacOS/Caret', so pgrep/ps matching on /Applications/Caret.app misses the host; use launchctl print's pid or lsof txt. A fresh VM guest makes no helper Jev request (no transfers), fill or first look.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"11ec014c3ef4eda5","sum":"Fill/gateway lore: memoryRefOf refs; >20-field forms fill in parts; joined fills keep caller identity; gateway.only names the provider; Laya fixture-only (422 >512 tokens, 5/min, slow-eval.sh). with-heavy: free disk minus --est-disk >= 8 GiB. Chrome insertText undo: closeTyping.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"9061cdc44b6fa399","sum":"C2/F2/GW1 fill lore: memory refs via memoryRefOf; forms over 20 fields split into parts accepted and undone alone; joined ambient fills promoted to explicit, keeping caller identity; gateway.only names the serving provider; Laya is fixture-only.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"9663e92a97e02b87","sum":"C2 fill lore: build Step.memory refs with memoryRefOf, never by hand; countries come only from closed state/province lists; forms over 20 fields split into parts of <=20, each accepted and undone alone; page-loop-eval retries Fill all after 500 ms.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"cc84b3cf81253ebf","sum":"C2: build Step.memory refs (id[#part][~option|~date]) with memoryRefOf(m, conversionOf(control)), never by hand; placeWithCountry adds a country only from the closed US-state/CA-province lists, for fields asksPlace accepts.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T085433Z-15cdbeee47a325f7","text":"C2: Step.memory refs are id[#part][~option|~date]; memoryWrites checks text exactly and only options/dates through their conversion. Build refs with memoryRefOf(m, conversionOf(control)), never by hand.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T085433Z-9b6840ae7771fd2d","text":"C2: placeWithCountry adds a country only by the closed US-state/CA-province lists and only for fields asksPlace accepts; the engine still needs exactly one loaded option equal to it. About country is deliberately not used.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d359c1b9ca63551e","sum":"C2: a page form over 20 fields is one goal with a segment per part of <=20 (reason moreFields), each run and undone on its own goalAccept; page-loop-eval's Fill all can race the page's ready-on-load fill, so it asks again after 500 ms.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T085433Z-a637346e142ef258","text":"C2: a page form over 20 fields is one goal with a segment per part of <=20 (page-planner parts, lower.ts cut, reason moreFields); each part runs only on its own goalAccept and undoes as task goal:sN. Fields past 4 parts are named as the user's.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T085434Z-d647567d5018f182","text":"C2: page-loop-eval's corpus Fill all can race the page's own ready-on-load fill (helper.fill returns null for a form in flight, no error); the row now asks again after 500 ms and logs it.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f8c7e4d7077b1a19","sum":"F2/GW1 fill and gateway lore: joined ambient fills are promoted to explicit; fill joins keep the caller's identity across waits; gateway.only names the serving provider; Laya is fixture-only (its endpoint permits training).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"bbf67222105d2e73","sum":"F2: fillRequest promotes a joined ambient flight to explicit before publishing, since ambient pop-ups fill no proposals. GW1: providerOptions.gateway.only names the serving provider from the model's endpoints API (laya-free is served by boundless).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T092359Z-18f5690369a8fa9a","text":"F2: fillRequest promotes a joined ambient flight to explicit before publication: ambient pop-ups do not populate proposals, so returning their FillProposal alone cannot serve handleFillAll. Different field scopes in one window wait and resolve fields again.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T094129Z-8c5d1007dd7df018","text":"GW1: the gateway serves convaiinnovations/laya-free through boundless, not convaiinnovations; providerOptions.gateway.only must use the serving provider listed by the model's endpoints API.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"79e694bb1404294d","sum":"GW1: Laya is fixture-only (its endpoint permits training): harnessEngine fixture provenance only, shipped apps refuse it. Fill joins compare selectedFormInputs after TabSource.readFor and keep the caller's reader/document/trigger identity across waits.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T100225Z-f4d02db1f4186bed","text":"GW1: Laya is fixture-only because its boundless endpoint permits training; use harnessEngine fixture provenance even with cache off. Generic clients without fixture provenance refuse it, and shipped-app markers always refuse it. Gateway Jev keeps normal sources.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T102153Z-a32a254ad92c6952","text":"Fill joins compare selectedFormInputs after TabSource.readFor: capped formFields can match scopes with different ranked controls. Preserve the caller reader/document/trigger identity across waits.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f3364d678b58484b","sum":"Free Laya 422s >512 tokens, JSON state, long options; 5 req/min: no Ask there (slow-eval.sh, laya.lock). Fill joins: one trigger, ordered inputs. with-heavy: free disk minus --est-disk >= 8 GiB; host build 3/2. Keep one of duplicate naps. Chrome insertText undo: closeTyping.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"97ddef9eec5e365c","sum":"A1/R1 Laya lore: free Laya 422s requests over ~512 tokens, JSON-object state and long choice options, and allows 5 req/min, so Ask cannot run on it; Ask scope is code's reading first (scope-reading.ts); run Laya evals via slow-eval.sh under laya.lock.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b49778a23660a963","sum":"A1: free Laya 422s requests over ~512 input tokens and allows 5 req/min, so Ask cannot run on it; Ask scope is code's reading first (planner/scope-reading.ts), the heads 'reading' question confirms it, and ask-reading-eval.ts scores readings with no model.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T102251Z-3a116bbdf83faf20","text":"A1: free Laya (gateway, boundless) 422s any request over ~512 input tokens (489 ok, ~519 not) and allows 5 req/min per team; heads and corpus fill requests are ~2000 tokens, so the Ask path cannot run on Laya as built (evidence/screen/a1/laya-limits.txt).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T102251Z-6d4e95952b64681c","text":"A1: Ask scope is code's reading first (planner/scope-reading.ts; any unread word means no reading); the heads 'reading' question confirms it and intent.agreed skips confirmScope/sectionScope. ask-reading-eval.ts scores readings with no model.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7bb813feffb3f3c1","sum":"R1: free Laya 422s JSON-object state and choice options over ~300 chars, so Ask-led evals there mostly fail; helper/scripts/slow-eval.sh runs eval sets on Laya in the background (a 429 ends the pass); queue on lockf -k ~/.caret-run/locks/laya.lock.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T102855Z-241459cd7cad2754","text":"R1: free Laya gives HTTP 422 for a JSON-object state (harness.ts layaState sends JSON text) and for a choice question whose options total over ~300 chars (heads' scope: 634), so Ask-led evals on Laya are mostly rejected (evidence/screen/r1/probe).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T102855Z-7e60ee41200b62c5","text":"R1: helper/scripts/slow-eval.sh runs all eval sets on Laya in the background; a 429 ends the pass and the set reruns from the replay cache. Other Laya users queue on lockf -k ~/.caret-run/locks/laya.lock; rejected requests replay from cache/failures.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"74a3e62ead206367","sum":"Fill joins need one trigger and ordered selectedFormInputs. with-heavy needs free disk minus --est-disk >= 8 GiB (swap counts): ask 3 mem/2 disk for a host build. Merged v2/* may hold a note in two naps; keep one. Chrome joins insertText to the typing undo step: closeTyping.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8208911c044286ba","sum":"Fill joins need the same trigger and ordered selectedFormInputs. H13: with-heavy refuses unless free disk minus --est-disk stays >= 8 GiB (swap growth counts), so ask the smallest honest estimate (a host build: 3 mem / 2 disk).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T114711Z-5f2b276e7a41de4a","text":"Fill joins require the same trigger and ordered selectedFormInputs: descriptor admission can omit different fields even when input sets match. Different triggers wait with their own captured identity.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T132506Z-afeea7cd00f9f436","text":"H13: with-heavy refuses unless free disk minus your --est-disk stays >= 8 GiB, so at about 10 GiB free a 2 GiB build waits; ask for the smallest honest estimate (harness build 3 mem / 2 disk), and swap growth on this Mac eats the same disk.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2aa517edf32bae42","sum":"I7: merged v2/* can hold one note in naps on both sides; keep one nap. a1-ask-reading once lost names at load ~11. Chrome joins insertText to the open typing undo step (one Cmd-Z took typed text too); setting the caret by script first closes it (insert.ts closeTyping).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T133620Z-cd21a7d05fec9102","text":"I7: merged v2/* branches can hold the same notes in naps on both sides (clean git merge, wake shows them twice); find leaves in two .tree files, keep one nap. a1-ask-reading 'acts on code's reading' lost names once in a default-worker suite at load ~11.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T161827Z-f17cd09096e8e827","text":"Chrome joins execCommand('insertText') to the open typing undo step, so one Cmd-Z also removed typed text in a contenteditable. Setting the caret by script where it already is closes the step: extension/src/content/insert.ts closeTyping.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
